WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.043
Safex

00:00:03.193 --> 00:00:06.463
After they were set up
by Eliza's family,

00:00:06.613 --> 00:00:09.940
Candy and Annie
had to sleep in the tree house.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:14.505
They were immersed
in the memories from Pony's Home.

00:00:14.655 --> 00:00:19.379
Actually, they could feel more happiness
when nobody bothered them.

00:00:20.654 --> 00:00:26.684
A dangerous garden party.

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:45.805
The sun is up already.

00:00:47.581 --> 00:00:50.106
We stayed chatting too late last night.

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:53.582
Let's get up now or Stear will tease us.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.622
What a wonderful feeling!

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:05.658
Good morning, Mr. Bird!

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.157
Candy, it's not good!

00:01:07.307 --> 00:01:08.429
What's wrong, Annie?

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.929
The rope ladder is gone!

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.402
Candy is frightened.

00:01:23.552 --> 00:01:25.006
Let me see, Brother!

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.185
It's great!

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.691
It must be those two!

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:38.624
Candy, what should we do?

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:42.097
Don't be afraid, Annie.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.163
I am so scared.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:49.104
Good morning, lazy bone!

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:50.548
Stear!

00:01:50.698 --> 00:01:52.269
Archie!

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.309
What's wrong, Annie?

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:58.105
The rope ladder is gone.

00:01:58.255 --> 00:01:59.875
It must be Eliza and her brother.

00:02:00.025 --> 00:02:00.940
Maybe.

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:02.508
Don't worry.

00:02:02.658 --> 00:02:07.355
I was prepared for this
since I was a child.

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:08.925
Look up.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.266
This tree house is very well equipped!

00:02:18.038 --> 00:02:21.106
Eliza, there is another rope ladder
in the tree house!

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.568
How come?

00:02:29.683 --> 00:02:31.981
It didn't work out again.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:37.379
Don't be too happy.
I won't let you go so easily.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:51.193
It feels so exciting
to live in a tree house!

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.297
Today is your last day here.

00:02:54.447 --> 00:02:58.639
Do we have to go back
to the hospital tonight, Candy?

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:03.237
Brother, don't feel so sad.

00:03:03.387 --> 00:03:05.016
We will meet again in the future.

00:03:05.986 --> 00:03:07.007
That's true.

00:03:07.157 --> 00:03:10.477
Candy can visit with Annie
whenever she has a vacation.

00:03:10.627 --> 00:03:13.055
Thank you, Archie.

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:17.553
Let's go to the lake after we eat.

00:03:17.703 --> 00:03:19.619
I have a new invention.

00:03:19.769 --> 00:03:21.301
And we can swim, too.

00:03:23.103 --> 00:03:25.328
But I don't have a swimsuit.

00:03:25.478 --> 00:03:28.407
Candy, you can borrow one of mine.

00:03:28.742 --> 00:03:30.767
That's perfect! Then I'm coming too!

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.722
There is a lake in the woods!

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.584
Hold on, Candy! Hide!

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.627
Grand Aunt Elroy?

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.723
What happened, Brother?

00:04:11.923 --> 00:04:17.219
The thing Grand Aunt Elroy sat on
was my invention.

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:31.227
It's broken!

00:04:31.377 --> 00:04:33.129
What is this thing, Stear?

00:04:33.279 --> 00:04:35.036
Listen, everyone.

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:37.736
This is a... bed in the water.

00:04:39.079 --> 00:04:40.740
A bed in the water?

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.883
This box is transparent
and is made out of artificial fiber.

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:49.182
A person can lie inside
and sink into the lake.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:53.847
There is a tube for breathing,
and there is a periscope, too.

00:04:54.697 --> 00:04:57.854
It seems like your new invention
is down the drain...

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.490
What did you say, Archie?!

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.005
Stear, don't get mad.
I would like to try it.

00:05:04.225 --> 00:05:07.765
Ok.
I'll make a double bed next time.

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:42.230
Let's have a party! How is that?

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.100
Agreed!

00:05:44.511 --> 00:05:46.843
Forget it.

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:50.338
Eliza!

00:05:50.488 --> 00:05:53.845
The four of you
can come to my dinner party.

00:05:53.995 --> 00:05:55.580
A dinner party?

00:05:56.389 --> 00:06:00.382
Yes, I invited many friends.

00:06:00.532 --> 00:06:03.091
Grand Aunt Elroy agreed with it.

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:06.683
What trick are you playing, Eliza?

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:09.259
Don't come if you don't want to.

00:06:09.409 --> 00:06:11.370
I was just being nice.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.600
Wait, Eliza!

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.699
- We are happy to come!
- Candy!

00:06:16.849 --> 00:06:20.043
A part of only four people is not fun.

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:23.679
I'll be waiting for you, hurry up!

00:06:25.919 --> 00:06:27.208
Candy!

00:06:27.358 --> 00:06:30.449
We don't know
what Eliza really wants.

00:06:31.191 --> 00:06:33.416
We are about to leave.

00:06:33.566 --> 00:06:35.886
Eliza won't do anything to us.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:41.657
Candy, I'll go with you.
Let me lend you my formal dress.

00:06:41.807 --> 00:06:42.823
Thank you, Annie.

00:06:42.973 --> 00:06:44.460
Let's go change our clothes.

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:51.275
Let's see, which one suits you best?

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:56.674
My suitcase is gone!

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:00.583
Gone?

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:04.680
Could it be...

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:35.820
They must be worried to death.

00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:42.681
Aren't they going to come?

00:07:42.831 --> 00:07:46.993
Candy never backs down,
she will come.

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:49.563
That's right.
She will make a fool of herself!

00:07:57.309 --> 00:08:00.843
Everyone, this is Candy and Annie.

00:08:01.648 --> 00:08:04.446
I am Candy! Nice to meet you!

00:08:04.884 --> 00:08:05.842
I am Annie.

00:08:07.087 --> 00:08:10.444
Candy, Annie, didn't I tell you
this is a dinner party?

00:08:10.594 --> 00:08:14.716
It's rude to dress like this.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.061
Now I see what's going on.

00:08:25.271 --> 00:08:27.496
Eliza, forgive them.

00:08:27.646 --> 00:08:31.634
How could an orphan from Pony's Home
have a formal dress to wear?

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:34.779
I...

00:08:37.717 --> 00:08:40.982
Annie, we must keep our dignity.

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:42.821
Welcome, everybody.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.024
Stear, Archie.

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:54.693
Don't feel restrained
in an Adley's party.

00:09:01.274 --> 00:09:03.442
I think so, too!

00:09:06.012 --> 00:09:07.445
You are...

00:09:08.281 --> 00:09:10.476
He is my cousin.

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:16.011
I am Michael. I am on leave right now,
so I came to join this party.

00:09:17.023 --> 00:09:19.748
A soldier from the French war zone?

00:09:19.898 --> 00:09:21.486
Michael is an army doctor.

00:09:22.762 --> 00:09:24.496
He is not a real doctor yet.

00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:32.261
We have an apprentice nurse here, too.
Mr. Michael.

00:09:32.538 --> 00:09:34.060
Miss Candy over there.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.572
You?

00:09:38.511 --> 00:09:40.033
Yes.

00:09:40.183 --> 00:09:43.569
She is the foster child of the Adleys,
and not attending her duties.

00:09:43.719 --> 00:09:45.446
That is awful.

00:09:45.718 --> 00:09:48.095
That's not awful, that's good!

00:09:48.245 --> 00:09:50.676
We need more nurses.

00:09:50.826 --> 00:09:53.281
It must a tough job serving at the frontline.

00:09:53.793 --> 00:09:56.853
I am going back to the battlefield
right after my leave ends.

00:09:58.331 --> 00:09:59.696
The battlefield?

00:09:59.966 --> 00:10:02.901
Michael, stop talking about the war.
Let's dance.

00:10:05.104 --> 00:10:07.863
Eliza, give Annie back her suitcase.

00:10:08.013 --> 00:10:11.273
It's in the room on the top floor.
Help yourself.

00:10:13.012 --> 00:10:14.912
The room on the top floor?

00:11:00.426 --> 00:11:01.757
Here!

00:11:19.445 --> 00:11:20.707
I found it!

00:11:30.389 --> 00:11:32.979
Open the door!

00:11:33.129 --> 00:11:34.518
Be quiet!

00:11:34.668 --> 00:11:37.358
It's you, Neal!
Why did you close the door?

00:11:38.631 --> 00:11:41.756
Candy, don't you like to take risks?

00:11:41.906 --> 00:11:44.959
The door is locked, use the rope.

00:11:45.109 --> 00:11:46.538
The rope?

00:11:49.575 --> 00:11:51.873
Or stay here and cry!

00:12:07.026 --> 00:12:08.994
It's so high.

00:12:10.363 --> 00:12:12.761
But I can't give up.

00:12:22.942 --> 00:12:24.070
Watch me.

00:12:41.094 --> 00:12:42.852
Ok.

00:13:16.429 --> 00:13:18.329
Isn't that Candy?

00:13:23.569 --> 00:13:25.134
Candy

00:13:26.005 --> 00:13:28.303
Why is Candy on the top floor?

00:13:28.708 --> 00:13:30.764
Everyone, look!

00:13:30.914 --> 00:13:33.236
Is this what an Adley's lady
should be doing?

00:13:33.386 --> 00:13:35.301
So undisciplined!

00:13:35.451 --> 00:13:37.307
So behined.

00:13:37.457 --> 00:13:40.710
She's almost like a monkey, shame on her!

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:43.553
How would Eliza have a relative like this?

00:14:07.113 --> 00:14:08.336
Candy!

00:14:08.486 --> 00:14:12.406
You must have never seen
a woman like this, right, Michael?

00:14:12.885 --> 00:14:14.778
Why is she like this?

00:14:14.928 --> 00:14:16.712
She is always like this.

00:14:16.862 --> 00:14:19.908
Liar! It must be a trick you
are playing, am I right?

00:14:21.661 --> 00:14:23.925
I don't know anything.

00:14:26.132 --> 00:14:30.858
Brother, we can't let
Grand Aunt Elroy see this.

00:14:31.108 --> 00:14:35.138
Ok, I will take care of that.

00:14:36.442 --> 00:14:39.742
Candy, slowly!

00:14:52.358 --> 00:14:55.452
Archie told me to go down fast. Ok!

00:14:57.963 --> 00:15:00.454
It's not like that, Candy!

00:15:01.333 --> 00:15:03.093
Throw down the suitcase!

00:15:17.216 --> 00:15:19.547
I can't just stand here.

00:15:20.986 --> 00:15:23.750
Leave her alone, Michael.

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:26.458
You are so heartless.

00:15:35.601 --> 00:15:38.598
What is that noise outside?

00:15:40.072 --> 00:15:42.003
It's nothing, Grand Aunt Elroy.

00:15:43.776 --> 00:15:47.671
Then why is it so noisy?

00:15:47.821 --> 00:15:51.872
The sunset is too beautiful,
and everyone is too excited.

00:15:52.022 --> 00:15:55.317
The sunset here is truly beautiful,
isn't it?

00:15:55.955 --> 00:15:57.780
You are right, Grand Aunt Elroy.

00:16:05.431 --> 00:16:07.831
Are you ok?

00:16:08.033 --> 00:16:09.257
Yes.

00:16:09.407 --> 00:16:11.925
Ok, let me come help you.

00:16:12.075 --> 00:16:13.561
Ok.

00:16:28.954 --> 00:16:30.717
It's ok now.

00:16:32.792 --> 00:16:34.516
Thanks.

00:16:34.666 --> 00:16:38.586
Candy, cherish your life.

00:16:38.898 --> 00:16:44.700
There are people dying
in the battlefield every day.

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:46.493
Sorry.

00:16:46.643 --> 00:16:51.665
There are still many important things
for us to work on together.

00:16:51.815 --> 00:16:52.933
Yes.

00:16:53.083 --> 00:16:55.775
Come on, let's go down.

00:17:04.123 --> 00:17:05.750
It's pissing me off!

00:17:23.776 --> 00:17:27.240
Damn! We tried everything!

00:17:36.121 --> 00:17:37.547
Brother.

00:17:37.697 --> 00:17:40.016
Candy is falling for Michael.

00:17:40.166 --> 00:17:42.614
We can't do anything, Archie.

00:17:42.764 --> 00:17:45.219
Michael is truly outstanding.

00:17:48.667 --> 00:17:52.426
Mr. Michael!

00:17:54.006 --> 00:17:56.426
A telegram from France.

00:17:57.146 --> 00:17:58.940
What?

00:18:03.148 --> 00:18:04.308
Everybody,

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:07.212
I was very glad to join this party.

00:18:07.419 --> 00:18:09.611
But I have to go back
to the battlefield right now.

00:18:09.761 --> 00:18:11.189
The battlefield?

00:18:11.991 --> 00:18:15.188
There are many patients waiting
for me to go back.

00:18:18.097 --> 00:18:22.295
There are many young people like us
in the battlefield.

00:18:22.701 --> 00:18:27.695
Some died, some are seriously wounded.

00:18:34.313 --> 00:18:36.804
I have to go back to the hospital, too.

00:18:37.049 --> 00:18:38.679
I'll give you a ride.

00:18:40.119 --> 00:18:41.545
Thanks a lot.

00:18:41.695 --> 00:18:43.121
Candy

00:18:44.223 --> 00:18:48.284
There are many patients waiting for me too.
See you again, Annie!

00:18:49.895 --> 00:18:51.321
Archie, Stear.

00:18:51.471 --> 00:18:54.194
Thanks for your hospitality.

00:18:55.234 --> 00:18:57.395
Bye, Candy!

00:18:59.138 --> 00:19:01.402
Eliza, good-bye.

00:19:02.942 --> 00:19:05.103
- Let's go, Candy.
- Alright.

00:19:13.485 --> 00:19:15.214
Michael...

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:25.356
Can we just waste our lives
with no goals every day?

00:19:44.283 --> 00:19:48.083
Are you scared in the battlefield?

00:19:48.287 --> 00:19:53.418
Of course! But the soldiers
are even more scared than I am.

00:20:02.334 --> 00:20:04.325
Let's say good-bye here.

00:20:05.604 --> 00:20:06.769
Alright.

00:20:07.506 --> 00:20:09.331
Maybe we won't be able to see
each other again.

00:20:09.481 --> 00:20:12.269
We medical people must fulfil our jobs.

00:20:15.547 --> 00:20:17.047
Take care, Candy!

00:20:18.517 --> 00:20:20.080
You too!

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:30.722
Bye, Candy!

00:20:31.663 --> 00:20:34.632
Bye, Mr. Michael!

00:20:38.837 --> 00:20:40.129
Good-bye!

00:20:44.843 --> 00:20:48.370
Mr. Michael,
I will be an outstanding nurse.

00:20:51.316 --> 00:20:53.477
This young man Michael

00:20:53.886 --> 00:21:01.452
firmly strengthened Candy's dream
of becoming a real nurse.
